{#
    One line of the proposed finishing order.

    Included twice — once for the places that score, once inside the disclosure
    that holds everyone else — so the two tables cannot drift apart.

    Nothing here is editable. The finishing order is the bracket's, and the
    bracket has been right about it eighteen times out of eighteen; the rank is
    shown rather than offered. What *does* change these rows is the decisions
    above, because a name resolved to a different blader changes the name here
    and an entrant dropped as "not a person" moves everyone below them up.

    The Challonge column is stated, not flagged. It differing from the blader
    column is the alias table working — `Sanya0207` is the Challonge account
    the bracket rendered in place of `Sanya` — and painting the normal case in
    warning colours teaches people to ignore the colour. The one row worth
    noticing is the one with no answer yet, and that is in red.
#}
<tr class="{{ placement.bladerName is null ? 'bg-heat-strong/5' }}">
    <td class="text-center">
        {% if placement.scores %}
            <twig:RankMedal :rank="placement.position" />
        {% else %}
            <span class="text-xs text-ink-ghost">{{ placement.position }}</span>
        {% endif %}
    </td>
    <td class="font-bold {{ placement.bladerName is null ? 'text-heat' : (placement.wonTheKnockout ? 'text-flame' : 'text-ink') }}">
        {{ placement.bladerName ?? placement.challongeName }}
        {% if placement.bladerName is null %}
            <twig:Badge tone="heat" size="sm">Undecided</twig:Badge>
        {% elseif placement.isNewBlader %}
            <twig:Badge tone="brand" size="sm">New</twig:Badge>
        {% elseif placement.wonTheKnockout %}
            <twig:Badge tone="positive" size="sm">KO</twig:Badge>
        {% endif %}
    </td>
    <td class="hidden font-mono text-xs text-ink-faint sm:table-cell">{{ placement.challongeName }}</td>
    <td class="text-center tabular-nums {{ placement.f1Points > 0 ? 'text-ink-body' : 'text-ink-ghost' }}">{{ placement.f1Points }}</td>
    <td class="hidden text-center sm:table-cell">
        <twig:BonusPoints :value="placement.bonusPoints" />
    </td>
    <td class="pr-4 text-right font-black tabular-nums {{ placement.scores ? 'text-ink' : 'text-ink-ghost' }}">{{ placement.totalPoints }}</td>
</tr>
